  "class": "wizard",
  "spellcastingAbility": "int",
  "background": "archaeologist",
  "backstory": "Deep within the sun-drenched vales of the Stoutlands, while others of his kin were content to tend to their barley and brew, the halfling who would eventually discard his name was busy unearthing the bones of the past. He was born with a shovel in one hand and an insatiable hunger for what lay beneath the loam. His transition into the arcane arts was not born of academic wonder, but of ruthless pragmatism; after discovering a singed, leather-bound grimoire in the crumbling remains of a long-forgotten barrow, he realized that magic was the ultimate tool for a tomb-breaker. To him, spells are not mysteries of the cosmos, but silver keys and invisible hands used to bypass the ancient wards that guard the world's hidden treasures.\n\nHe moves through the world under a shroud of anonymity, a nameless shadow in the dusty corners of great libraries and the mud-slicked trenches of excavation sites. His ambition is singularly focused on the legendary Scepter of the Obsidian King, a relic spoken of in hushed whispers by those who study the dead. While others might seek such an item to restore a kingdom or honor a legacy, he sees only the staggering weight of its platinum filigree and the black-market fortunes it would command in the hands of a desperate collector. To him, history is not a teacher, but a vault waiting to be emptied, and he views every traveling companion as a potential thief waiting to snatch the glory and gold of his next great discovery.",
  "alignment": "neutral_good",
  "name": "joli",
